Q: This Activity already has an action bar supplied by the window decor
A: <p>I think you're developing for Android Lollipop, but anyway include this line:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;item name="windowActionBar"&gt;false&lt;/item&gt; 
</code></pre>

<p>to your theme declaration inside of your <code>app/src/main/res/values/styles.xml</code>.</p>

<p>Also, if you're using <code>AppCompatActivity</code> support library of version 22.1 or greater, add this line:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;item name="windowNoTitle"&gt;true&lt;/item&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>Your theme declaration may look like this after all these additions:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;!-- Base application theme. --&gt;
&lt;style name="AppTheme" parent="Theme.AppCompat.Light.DarkActionBar"&gt;
    &lt;!-- Customize your theme here. --&gt;
    &lt;item name="colorPrimary"&gt;@color/colorPrimary&lt;/item&gt;
    &lt;item name="colorPrimaryDark"&gt;@color/colorPrimaryDark&lt;/item&gt;
    &lt;item name="colorAccent"&gt;@color/colorAccent&lt;/item&gt;
    &lt;item name="windowActionBar"&gt;false&lt;/item&gt;
    &lt;item name="windowNoTitle"&gt;true&lt;/item&gt;
&lt;/style&gt;
</code></pre>

