Q: Perform Migration when Deploying to Azure, SQLite/.NET Core
A: <p>I followed a few suggestions on the web and finally found a solution that works for me. You can create a method called UpdateDatabase (or any other name you want) and call it in the Configure part of the Startup.cs.</p>

<pre><code>private void UpdateDatabase(IApplicationBuilder app)
{
    using (var serviceScope = app.ApplicationServices.GetRequiredService&lt;IServiceScopeFactory&gt;().CreateScope())
    {
        // get your database context of the current app
        using (var context = serviceScope.ServiceProvider.GetService&lt;InsertYourDbContext&gt;())
        {
            // Call the migrate of the database provider to
            // apply all data migrations pending
            context.Database.Migrate();
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>

