Q: How do I reference Entity Framework 6 from a .NET core class library in RC2?
A: <p>Entity Framework 6.1.3 does not support .NET Core. This was part of the motivation for creating Entity Framework Core. EF 6 has deep ties to APIs in .NET Framework that may not be ported to exist in .NET Core.</p>

<p>You can still use EF6 with "project.json" projects but you need to target .NET Framework instead of .NET Core.</p>

<pre><code>{
    "dependencies": {
        "EntityFramework": "6.1.3"
    },
    "frameworks": {
        "net461": { }
    }
}
</code></pre>

Q: Does Entity Framework 6 support .Net 3.5?
A: <p>On the right hand side of the <a href="https://entityframework.codeplex.com/wikipage?title=Roadmap">EF6 Roadmap page on CodePlex</a> it says that .Net 4.0 is the System Requirement. Furthermore, when <a href="https://entityframework.codeplex.com/sourcecontrol/latest#src/EntityFramework/EntityFramework.csproj">reviewing the <code>csproj</code> files associated with EF6</a>, it appears that only 4.0 and 4.5 are supplied as targets:</p>

<pre><code>    ...
    &lt;CodeAnalysisRuleSet&gt;..\Strict.ruleset&lt;/CodeAnalysisRuleSet&gt;
  &lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
  &lt;PropertyGroup Condition=" '$(Configuration)|$(Platform)' == 'Release|AnyCPU' "&gt;
    &lt;TargetFrameworkVersion&gt;v4.5&lt;/TargetFrameworkVersion&gt;
    ...
  &lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
  &lt;PropertyGroup Condition=" '$(Configuration)|$(Platform)' == 'DebugNet40|AnyCPU' "&gt;
    &lt;TargetFrameworkVersion&gt;v4.0&lt;/TargetFrameworkVersion&gt;
    ...
</code></pre>

<p>In light of this I would say the answer is <strong>No: EF6 does not support .Net 3.5</strong>.</p>
